<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104861" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίγληνος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> as epith. of ear-rings, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕρματα τρίγληνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.183
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.298
			</span></i>: ancient critics (cf. Sch. ad loc.) expld. it (<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>) from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλήνεα</span> (<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.192
			</span></i>), 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀξιοθέατα</span>
			, or (<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>) 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίκοκκα</span>
			, i. e. with three berry-shaped ornaments, or (<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>) 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τριῶν ζῳδίων
				συγκείμενα</span>
			, or (<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>) 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριόφθαλμα</span>
			, like
			
				Att.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριοττίδες</span>; and in other ways. It
			is prob. formed from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλήνη</span> as
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίκλινος</span> fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλίνη,</span> etc., but the sense remains
			uncertain. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>three-eyed,</i> of Hecate, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				7.325a
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
